def spaced(text):
 """Format prose without rewriting commands, links or filesystem paths."""
 import re
 parts=re.split(r'(```[\s\S]*?```|`[^`]+`|https?://[^\s<)]+|(?<!\w)/[A-Za-z0-9._/\-]+)',text)
 return ''.join(part if i%2 else spaced_prose(part) for i,part in enumerate(parts))
def spaced_prose(text):
 # Space compact prose while preserving category IDs, filenames and 4B-style labels.
 import re
 text=re.sub(r'(?<=\d)(?=[a-z]{2,})',' ',text)
 protected={'BF','NVFP','NF','FP','INT','IQ','GLiDEv','python'}
 text=re.sub(r'\b([A-Za-z]{2,})(?=\d)(?!\d+_)',lambda m:m[1] if m[1] in protected else m[1]+' ',text)
 text=re.sub(r'\b([Aa])(?=\d)',r'\1 ',text)
 text=re.sub(r'(?<=%)(?=[A-Za-z])',' ',text)
 text=re.sub(r',(?=[A-Za-z])',', ',text)
 text=re.sub(r'(?<=[a-z]\.)(?=\d)',' ',text)
 for old,new in [('GLiDEv','GLiDE v'),('System1','System 1'),('to+','to +'),('percentagepoints','percentage points'),('andSonnet','and Sonnet'),('small:147','small: 147'),('spans-','spans -'),('from-','from -'),('2.3BF16','2.3 BF16'),('2.2NVFP4','2.2 NVFP4'),('categories(', 'categories ('),('),40', '), 40'),('models,3','models, 3'),('questions,41','questions, 41'),(';206','; 206'),('Artemis\'s1','Artemis\'s 1'),('**1290','** 1290'),('%),310','%), 310')]:text=text.replace(old,new)
 return text
METHOD='''Every main configuration has1,934 selected primary responses across41categories. Strict accuracy counts a wrong usable answer and an unsuccessful response as unsuccessful in the same fixed denominator. Input limits, declared refusals, rate/service failures and other errors are shown separately. They do not establish what an unserved model would have answered.

The1,342 original inputs remain exact. Six existing categories(F26–F31) gain32questions each, growing from8to40. Ten practical categories(P01–P10) add40questions each. The120 companion diagnostics remain separate. The downloadable native JSONL preserves all original envelopes, including206 legacy packets; use native_input verbatim for faithful replay. Category IDs are authoritative. P07 and P10 retain older wording aliases in source metadata; question membership is unchanged.

This is a post-measurement presentation cutoff: unrounded correct/n must be at least62%. The same26model set appears in every main graph, category table, leader list and relative-profile analysis. Individual category scores below62% remain visible. All38v2measurements remain in all_statistics.json. Kev4B and H2O Lightning Nemotron are explicitly retired from the main selection; AutoThink is an adaptive archival reference. Qwen, plain H2O and older Jev remain historical; only Jev1.14 is current. Models tested only on the older bank have no inferred v2score.

For unchanged configurations, recorded exact baseline and expansion inputs are reused, including304Microsoft development responses. Upgraded defaults use the authorized full-bank runs; Fastino's current catalog-declared v2.3BF16 replaces the earlier v2.2NVFP4 measurement. Returned identities and source fingerprints are recorded in model_metadata.json; aliases and captured metadata are not independent attestation of hidden weights. Trio's native request alias resolved to the same returned dated version. No failed question was shortened, and no scored retry or best-of selection replaced a primary response. Busy-service backoff applied only before unattempted Drex/Clef inputs; all first failures remain recorded.

Timing distributions pool individual primary complete-response client times; phase/category medians and p95s are never averaged. Network is included; preparation, loading, warmups, queueing and cooldowns are excluded. Providers, precision, concurrency, routes and dates differ. Retained baseline and new timings can span sessions. Quick failures can reduce all-primary latency; usable-only medians are exported separately. These are service measurements, not isolated architecture-speed comparisons.

Native closed-choice counters vary by provider and are not uniformly generated reasoning tokens. Trio does not report this counter. Sol used reasoning none; Opus5used thinking disabled with JSON choices; Sonnet5.5used its verified no-thinking between_tools configuration with no tools supplied. These are the only three main LLM references. The adaptive AutoThink result is preserved outside the main System1 view.

The local deployment was selected as an accessible older setup. Owner records identify an RTX2060with6GB VRAM; current API evidence attests CUDA, allocation and model digests without independently identifying the physical GPU product. Context and quantization belong to each measured configuration. Local hardware/electricity cost is unmeasured. A complete1,934-call monetary cost ledger has not been consolidated; older1,342-call tariffs are not scaled into a new v2bank price.

The bank includes related generated variants and model-guided development, including Jev and retained Microsoft/Drex feedback. It is a development benchmark, not an independently sampled intelligence or deployment-safety test. Fresh held-out items and repeatability measurements are needed for broader generalization. The public export contains answer-free questions, aggregate correctness and per-input timing/status/hash evidence. The scoring key, model choices, probabilities and per-question correctness remain private under the established release policy. Offline public checks reproduce coverage, timing and aggregate consistency; they cannot independently rescore hidden answers.
'''
CSS='''body{font:16px/1.55 system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;color:#17212c;margin:0;background:#f5f7f9}main{max-width:1400px;margin:auto;padding:36px 24px;background:white}h1{font-size:36px;line-height:1.15}h2{margin-top:40px}h3{margin-top:26px}a{color:#16728c}nav{display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:24px 0}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px;margin:15px 0}td,th{padding:9px 11px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde3e8;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}th{background:#eef2f5;white-space:nowrap}td:first-child{font-weight:600}img{width:100%;height:auto}details{border:1px solid #dce3e8;border-radius:8px;margin:12px 0;padding:14px}summary{font-weight:650;cursor:pointer}.muted{color:#596675;font-size:14px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr));gap:14px}.card{padding:18px;background:#edf4f6;border-top:4px solid #16728c}.card strong{font-size:25px;display:block}.local td:first-child{border-left:5px solid #7c3aed}.reference td:first-child{border-left:5px solid #d5b34e;background:#fff9e5}.hosted td:first-child{border-left:5px solid #16728c}input,select{font:inherit;padding:9px;border:1px solid #aebac4;border-radius:5px;margin:5px 0 12px}blockquote{margin-left:0;padding:12px 18px;border-left:3px solid #cbd6df;background:#f7f9fa;font-size:14px}.legend{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap}.swatch{display:inline-block;width:12px;height:12px;margin-right:6px}code{font-size:.9em}.finding{border-left:4px solid #16728c;padding-left:16px}@media(max-width:650px){main{padding:24px 14px}h1{font-size:28px}}'''
