 catalogue='# V2 results outside the main comparison\n\nThe62% cutoff is a reporting selection. Measurements are retained; no scores were changed. AutoThink is archival; Kev4B and H2O Lightning Nemotron are explicitly retired from the main view. No graphs appear in this catalogue.\n\n'+mdtable(['Configuration','Correct','Accuracy','Usable','Reason','Coverage'],exclusion_rows(all_s))+'\n\n## Historical only: not evaluated on v2\n\nThese models have only1,342-question results. They are not ranked against1,934-question models, and their v2scores are unknown.\n\n'+mdtable(['Configuration','Historical correct','Historical accuracy'],[(r['label'],f"{r['correct']}/{r['n']}",pct(r['accuracy'])) for r in load(SOURCE/'historical_only.json')])+f'\n\n[Older below-50% trials and formats]({SITE}local_updates_2026-10-31/below_50.html) retain their original sample sizes.\n'
 write(dest/'not_in_main.md',spaced(catalogue));write(dest/'not_in_main.html','<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>System1v2:models outside the main comparison</title><style>'+CSS+'</style><main>'+markdown(spaced(catalogue),extensions=['tables'])+'<p><a href="report.html">Main v2comparison</a></p></main></html>')
 if publish:
  rows=[(m['label'],m['role'],f"{m['correct']}/1934",pct(m['accuracy']),f"{m['median_ms']:.0f} ms",f"{m['p95_ms']:.0f} ms") for m in s['models'].values()]
  readme='# System 1 Decision Benchmark v2\n\n**1,934questions across41categories.26configurations meet the62% overall reporting cutoff:**20hosted decision models,3local configurations and3selected reasoning-disabled LLM references. Updated November1,2026.\n\n**Fastino leads the observed overall score at82.89%; D3 Ultra leads the592additions at77.70%; StartLux Instant leads the measured local full-bank configurations at66.70%.** Fastino\'s six-answer margin over GPT-6 Sol does not establish a reliable accuracy advantage; its median response is216ms versus999ms.\n\n[Interactive report]('+SITE+'report.html) · [41named categories]('+SITE+'report.html#functions) · [Model strengths and weaknesses]('+SITE+'report.html#profiles) · [Other models and historical scopes]('+SITE+NAME+'/not_in_main.html)\n\n![V2 qualifying configurations: hosted blue, local purple, reasoning-disabled LLM references gold](results/releases/'+NAME+'/accuracy_speed.png)\n\n## Main comparison\n\n'+mdtable(['Configuration','Setting','Correct','Accuracy','Median','p95'],rows)+'\n\nAll38v2measurements remain available. Main graphs, category tables and leaders use the same26-model qualifying set. Individual category scores can be below62%; the cutoff applies to overall accuracy. AutoThink is archival. Kev4B,Nemotron,Qwen,plain H2O and older Jev are outside the main selection; latest Jev1.14 is retained.\n\n## Questions, categories and analysis\n\nThe expansion adds192questions to six existing categories(F26–F31), bringing each from8to40, and400questions across ten new practical categories(P01–P10),40each. All1,342original native inputs remain exact.120companion diagnostics stay separate.\n\n- [Exact native JSONL](results/releases/'+NAME+'/questions_1934.jsonl), [CSV](results/releases/'+NAME+'/questions_1934.csv), [readable text](results/releases/'+NAME+'/questions_1934.txt) and [metadata](results/releases/'+NAME+'/metadata_core.jsonl)\n- [Category descriptions and scores](documents/FUNCTIONS.md), [v2design and selection](documents/V2_DESIGN.md), [analysis](results/releases/'+NAME+'/analysis.md) and [LLM settings](documents/LLM_REFERENCES.md)\n- [Main aggregates](results/releases/'+NAME+'/statistics.json), [all38records](results/releases/'+NAME+'/all_statistics.json), [category CSV](results/releases/'+NAME+'/category_scores.csv) and [model profiles](results/releases/'+NAME+'/model_profiles.csv)\n- [73,492answer-free timing/status records](results/releases/'+NAME+'/timing_evidence.csv.gz), [audit receipt](results/releases/'+NAME+'/audit_receipt.json) and [release checksums](results/releases/'+NAME+'/manifest.json)\n\n## Measurement limits\n\nPooled timing uses individual primary responses, including failures; phase/category medians are not averaged. Hardware, routes, precision and dates differ. Wrong answers are distinguished from context limits, refusals and service errors. A complete v2monetary ledger is not consolidated, and older tariffs are not extrapolated. Model-guided development and related variants limit generalization. Public data omits the scoring key, model choices and individual correctness; the answer key remains private under the existing policy.\n\n## Reproduce the publication offline\n\nThe [scripts/](scripts/README.md) use only public captures for validation and report rebuilding. No API keys or live inference are needed.\n\n```sh\npython3 -m pip install -r scripts/requirements-reports.txt python-dotenv\npython3 scripts/validate_system1_v2.py\npython3 -m unittest discover -s scripts -p "test_system1_v2.py"\npython3 scripts/publish_system1_v2.py --output /tmp/system1-v2-rebuild\n```\n\nHistorical check: `python3 scripts/validate_october21_release.py`. All dated v1releases and their original denominators remain archived. [Previous1,342-question report](results/releases/local_updates_2026-10-31/report.html).\n'
  # Markdown prose is spaced without rewriting code, IDs or relative targets.
  import re
  readme=re.sub(r'(^|\n)([^\n]+)',lambda match:match.group(0),readme)
  for old,new in [('1,934questions','1,934 questions'),('across41','across 41'),('26configurations','26 configurations'),('the62%','the 62%'),(':**20',':** 20'),('20hosted','20 hosted'),('3local','3 local'),('3selected','3 selected'),('November1,2026','November 1, 2026'),('at82.89%','at 82.89%'),('the592additions','the 592 additions'),('at77.70%','at 77.70%'),('at66.70%','at 66.70%'),('is216ms versus999ms','is 216 ms versus 999 ms'),('All38v2measurements','All 38 v2 measurements'),('same26-model','same 26-model'),('below62%','below 62%'),('Kev4B,Nemotron,Qwen,plain','Kev 4B, Nemotron, Qwen, plain'),('Jev1.14','Jev 1.14'),('adds192questions','adds 192 questions'),('from8to40','from 8 to 40'),('and400questions','and 400 questions'),('40each','40 each'),('All1,342original','All 1,342 original'),('exact.120companion','exact. 120 companion'),('41named','41 named'),('v2design','v2 design'),('all38records','all 38 records'),('73,492answer-free','73,492 answer-free'),('v2monetary','v2 monetary'),('v1releases','v1 releases'),('Previous1,342-question','Previous 1,342-question')]:readme=readme.replace(old,new)
  write(ROOT/'README.md',readme)
  functions='# System 1 v2: 41 categories\n\nAll category tables use the26configurations with at least62% overall. Low individual-category scores remain visible. [Current report]('+SITE+'report.html#functions) · [Category source data](../results/releases/'+NAME+'/category_scores.csv).\n\n'
  for fid in sorted(guide):
   g=guide[fid];functions+=f"## {fid} · {g['display_name']}\n\n{g['questions']}questions. {g['what_it_tests']}\n\nExample: {g['illustration']}\n\n"+mdtable(['Configuration','Correct','Accuracy'],[(s['models'][mid]['label'],lookup['correct']+'/'+lookup['n'],pct(float(lookup['accuracy']))) for mid in s['ranked_model_ids'] for lookup in [next(c for c in cats if c['model_id']==mid and c['family_id']==fid)]])+'\n'
  write(ROOT/'documents/FUNCTIONS.md',spaced(functions))
  write(ROOT/'documents/LLM_REFERENCES.md',spaced('# V2 reasoning-disabled LLM references\n\nOnly GPT-6 Sol, Claude Opus5 and Claude Sonnet5.5 are current LLM references. Qwen is historical and has no v2score.\n\n'+mdtable(['Reference','Correct /1934','Accuracy','Median','Control'],[(s['models'][mid]['label'],s['models'][mid]['correct'],pct(s['models'][mid]['accuracy']),f"{s['models'][mid]['median_ms']:.0f} ms",control) for mid,control in [('reference_sol','reasoning none; verified no reasoning output'),('reference_opus5','thinking disabled; JSON-choice;185declared refusals'),('reference_sonnet','between_tools no-thinking control; no tools; zero thinking verified')]])+'\n\nStrict accuracy retains refusals and service failures. These configurations do not measure the same models with reasoning enabled. Fastino leads Sol by six answers overall; paired exact p=.768 does not establish an accuracy advantage. Sol leads the equal-category and practical-addition scores. [Full methods](../results/releases/'+NAME+'/analysis.md).\n'))
  write(ROOT/'documents/OUTPUT_COMPLIANCE.md','# V2 output compliance and coverage\n\nAll1,934first responses remain in each model denominator. Wrong usable decisions are distinguished from input limits, refusals, service/rate limits and other failures.\n\n'+mdtable(['Model','Usable','Wrong usable','Failures'],[(s['models'][mid]['label'],f"{s['models'][mid]['valid']}/1934",s['models'][mid]['wrong_usable'],str(s['models'][mid]['failure_counts'])) for mid in mids_from(s)])+'\n\n[Interactive coverage analysis]('+SITE+'report.html#coverage) · [All v2measurements](../results/releases/'+NAME+'/all_statistics.json).\n')
  design='# System 1 Decision Benchmark v2: design and selection\n\nThe frozen core contains1,934questions,41categories and no replacement of the original1,342native inputs. Six existing categories(F26–F31) grow8→40by adding32each; ten new practical categories(P01–P10) add40each. The120diagnostics are separate.\n\nThe exact native JSONL is the authoritative replay format;206legacy envelopes remain unchanged. CSV and TXT support inspection. The public key is intentionally omitted under the established benchmark policy.\n\n## Practical categories\n\n'+mdtable(['ID','Category','Questions','Decision being tested'],[(fid,guide[fid]['display_name'],40,guide[fid]['what_it_tests']) for fid in sorted(guide) if fid.startswith('P')])+'\n\n## Inclusion\n\nThe final62% cutoff uses unrounded correct/n, including unsuccessful responses. A1,934-question model needs at least1,200correct. The same26configuration set is used for graphs, category scores, category leaders and relative profiles. Kev4B,Nemotron and adaptive AutoThink are explicitly outside this set. Qwen, plain H2O and Jev1.13 remain historical. The three LLM references are Sol,Opus5andSonnet5.5with reasoning disabled. All38v2records remain public separately. Older1,342-only scores are not converted or mixed into v2rankings.\n\n## Validity limits\n\nThe new questions were hardened and reviewed during model-guided development. Jev and retained Microsoft/Drex feedback are development exposure. Related variants, selected model feedback and a single recorded primary response per input limit independent generalization. Category specialties are descriptive and exploratory. Fixed-bank counts are exact; paired resampling explores hypothetical bank mixtures and does not measure inference repeatability. Full scoring-key and answer audits remain owner-side; public checks cover input hashes, coverage, timing and aggregate consistency.\n'
  write(ROOT/'documents/V2_DESIGN.md',spaced(design))
  write(ROOT/'data/README.md','# Benchmark data\n\nThe current v2core has **1,934questions across41categories**. Original inputs below remain archived unchanged.\n\n- [Exact native JSONL](../results/releases/'+NAME+'/questions_1934.jsonl)\n- [CSV](../results/releases/'+NAME+'/questions_1934.csv) and [readable text](../results/releases/'+NAME+'/questions_1934.txt)\n- [Item/category metadata](../results/releases/'+NAME+'/metadata_core.jsonl) and [bank manifest](../results/releases/'+NAME+'/bank_manifest.json)\n\nThe original1,342native inputs are preserved exactly.206legacy envelopes remain authoritative in JSONL. No scoring key, model choices or per-question correctness is published. [Results](../results/README.md).\n')
  write(ROOT/'results/README.md','# Results and evidence\n\n## Current: System 1 Decision Benchmark v2\n\n[26qualifying configurations on1,934questions and41categories](releases/'+NAME+'/report.html), using an exact62% overall cutoff.20hosted decision models,3locals and3reasoning-disabled LLM references.\n\n- [Main aggregates](releases/'+NAME+'/statistics.json) and [all38v2records](releases/'+NAME+'/all_statistics.json)\n- [Main model CSV](releases/'+NAME+'/model_statistics.csv), [category CSV](releases/'+NAME+'/category_scores.csv) and [profiles](releases/'+NAME+'/model_profiles.csv)\n- [Questions](releases/'+NAME+'/questions_1934.jsonl), [timing/status evidence](releases/'+NAME+'/timing_evidence.csv.gz), [audit](releases/'+NAME+'/audit_receipt.json) and [checksums](releases/'+NAME+'/manifest.json)\n- [Brief excluded-model and historical-only catalogue](releases/'+NAME+'/not_in_main.html)\n\n## Previous releases\n\n[October31:1,342-question v1comparison](releases/local_updates_2026-10-31/report.html) · [October30](releases/native_additions_2026-10-30/report.html) · [October29](releases/adaptive_additions_2026-10-29/report.html). All dated evidence and original denominators remain unchanged. Historical scores are not ranked against the larger v2bank.\n')
  write(ROOT/'documents/README.md','# Documents\n\n- [Current v2report]('+SITE+'report.html)\n- [41categories and scores](FUNCTIONS.md)\n- [V2design, expansion and model selection](V2_DESIGN.md)\n- [V2model analysis](../results/releases/'+NAME+'/analysis.md)\n- [Reasoning-disabled LLM references](LLM_REFERENCES.md)\n- [Coverage and output compliance](OUTPUT_COMPLIANCE.md)\n- [Other v2models and historical-only records](../results/releases/'+NAME+'/not_in_main.html)\n\nEarlier documents retain their dated scopes. [Original three-model reference](THREE_MODEL_REFERENCE.md) · [Local setup history](LOCAL_GPU_RUNS.md) · [Image capabilities](IMAGE_CAPABILITIES.md).\n')
  old=(ARCHIVE/'scripts/README.md.snapshot').read_text();write(ROOT/'scripts/README.md','# Benchmark scripts\n\n## Current v2publication\n\n`publish_system1_v2.py` rebuilds the26-model,1,934-question public report offline from sanitized captures. `validate_system1_v2.py` checks exact inputs,73,492timing records, aggregate/category totals,62% selection, privacy, links and seals. `test_system1_v2.py` checks cutoff boundaries and exclusions. `system1_v2_history.py` resolves pre-v2presentation snapshots for old validators. No inference or credentials are required.\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/validate_system1_v2.py\npython3 -m unittest discover -s scripts -p "test_system1_v2.py"\npython3 scripts/publish_system1_v2.py --output /tmp/system1-v2-rebuild\n```\n\n## Historical scripts and releases\n\n'+old)
